<title>USA: U.S. Boxed Beef cut-out at 1500 CDT - USDA.</title>
<headline>U.S. Boxed Beef cut-out at 1500 CDT - USDA.</headline>
<dateline>DES MOINES 1997-08-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Boxed beef firm on light to moderate demand and offerings. Select and Choice rib and round cuts generally steady, while loin cuts firm and chuck cuts higher.  Beef trimmings mostly steady on moderate demand and offerings. - USDA</p>
<p>------</p>
<p>202 Fab Lds  CH 1-3	CH 1-3	SE 1-3	SE 1-3</p>
<p> 42 50s Lds  550/700     700/850     550/700     700/850</p>
<p>4 Grd Lds ---------------------------------------------</p>
<p>Values =     103.69	103.30	 97.68	 95.45</p>
<p>Changes	   0.80	  0.55	  1.33	  0.40</p>
<p>Rib	  162.90	163.09	144.89	139.86</p>
<p>Chuck	 72.63	 71.08	 77.24	 71.64</p>
<p>Round	 90.43	 90.43	 88.24	 88.24</p>
<p>Loin	 162.75	162.98	139.66	139.58</p>
<p>Brisket     58.47	 58.47	 58.85	 58.85</p>
<p>Shrt Plate  63.19	 63.11	 63.43	 63.27</p>
<p>Flank	 57.70	 57.70	 56.76	 56.76</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk 312 408 8720))</p>
